# .gitignore
# ----------
# Files and folders Git should NEVER track. Each entry is explained so you
# know WHY it is excluded.

# --- Generated runtime output ----------------------------------------
# Logs and alerts are created when the NIDS runs. They are different on
# every machine and every run, so they must not be committed.
logs/
*.log
*.csv
# Exception: keep the sample blacklist, which IS source data we maintain.
!data/blacklist.txt

# --- Python bytecode cache -------------------------------------------
# Python compiles .py files to .pyc inside __pycache__ for speed. These are
# regenerated automatically and are machine-specific.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# --- Virtual environments --------------------------------------------
# Never commit an environment; others recreate it from requirements.txt.
# (We use a conda env named 'nids', but cover the common local-env folders too.)
.venv/
venv/
env/
.conda/

# --- Test / tooling caches -------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# --- IDE / editor settings -------------------------------------------
# Personal editor settings should not be forced on other contributors.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------
# Files the operating system drops into folders automatically.
Thumbs.db      # Windows image cache
desktop.ini    # Windows folder settings
.DS_Store      # macOS folder metadata

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------
# If you ever add a real secrets file, keep it out of Git. Commit .env.example
# (a template with blank values) instead.
.env
